[1m[38;5;231mWhich notification architecture should I design around?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mA: Fan-out on write (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mtask_events + one notifications row per subscriber, written in the same transaction. Per-item read state, cheap [39m
     [38;5;246mreads, write amplification at scale.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m B: Compute on read
     [38;5;246mJust task_events + a per-subscription read watermark. No write amplification, free history, but no per-item read [39m
     [38;5;246mstate.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m C: Direct insert, no event log
     [38;5;246mMutations write notifications rows directly. Simplest today; no activity history and fan-out logic duplicated per [39m
     [38;5;246mmutation.[39m
